You are a senior Supabase security engineer and PostgreSQL RLS expert.

Your task is to perform a full security audit and fix persistent bugs related to:

* Row Level Security (RLS)
* Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)
* Database access conflicts
* Storage permissions
* Messaging visibility
* Realtime subscription failures
* Recursive policy deadlocks
* Unauthorized data exposure

The application is ArtVault — a secure art storage and portfolio platform built entirely on Supabase.

Tech stack:

* Supabase Auth
* PostgreSQL
* Supabase RLS
* Supabase Storage
* Edge Functions
* Realtime subscriptions

Main objectives:

* Fix broken RLS policies
* Resolve RBAC permission conflicts
* Prevent unauthorized access or privilege escalation
* Preserve strict write protections
* Ensure users can securely access their own content
* Keep all fixes production-safe and least-privilege

Focus on:

1. RLS Policy Analysis

* Identify logical deadlocks caused by restrictive RLS policies
* Detect recursive policy dependencies
* Fix visibility issues for authenticated users
* Ensure newly created records remain visible to their owners
* Ensure policies work correctly for first-time users with no existing records

2. Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)
   Audit and fix role permission logic for:

* admin
* moderator
* authenticated users
* anonymous/public users
* artwork owners
* collaborators/shared access users

Verify:

* Users cannot access unauthorized artwork or private files
* Public users cannot access private records
* Moderators only access authorized moderation data
* Admin-only operations remain protected
* Role escalation is impossible
* Ownership checks using auth.uid() are properly enforced

3. Artwork & Storage Security
   Audit:

* artwork visibility rules
* private/public artwork access
* storage bucket policies
* upload permissions
* file ownership validation
* realtime subscriptions tied to artwork visibility

Verify:

* Private artwork is never publicly exposed
* Users can only modify their own files
* Shared/collaborative access works correctly
* Storage policies match database ownership rules
* Realtime subscriptions respect RLS permissions

4. Messaging & Visibility Bugs

* Newly created conversations may become invisible because of restrictive RLS conditions
* Conversation participants should always retain visibility
* Empty conversation threads should remain accessible to valid participants

Requirements:

* Review all affected RLS and RBAC policies
* Detect conflicting access chains
* Generate safe SQL migration patches
* Avoid broad USING (true) policies unless absolutely necessary
* Maintain least-privilege access principles
* Add comments explaining security decisions
* Suggest additional hardening improvements

Expected output:

1. Root cause analysis
2. RBAC security analysis
3. Proposed fix
4. SQL migration patch
5. Security impact assessment
6. Regression risks
7. Recommended follow-up improvements

Important constraints:

* Never expose private artwork or sensitive user metadata
* Never weaken UPDATE/DELETE protections unnecessarily
* Never allow unauthorized role escalation
* Never expose private storage objects publicly
* Keep all fixes production-safe
* Prefer explicit ownership checks using auth.uid()
